DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with --exec-mode
  for the vulnerable endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied URL query
  parameter flows directly into system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard in fn() event handler
              `if (exec_mode && mg_match(hm->uri, mg_str("/exec"), NULL))`
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hm->query (mongoose HTTP message)
  path:       fn() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts cmd via mg_http_get_var()
              the extracted string is passed directly to system()
  transforms: none — mg_http_get_var URL-decodes the param, no further processing

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — 3 hunks:
    1. global:              added `exec_mode` after s_port declaration
    2. handle_exec():       new function before fn(), extracts cmd and calls system()
    3. fn():                replaced direct serve_dir with exec_mode branch + serve_dir fallback
    4. main() arg parsing:  added --exec-mode flag handler

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./mongoose_server --port 18025 --root /tmp/www --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18025/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 404 (mg_http_serve_dir
               cannot find the file on disk).

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr (inherited fds), not the
    HTTP response body. The response body contains only "Command dispatched: <cmd>".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/pwned) to confirm blind execution.
  - mg_http_get_var() URL-decodes the query parameter before passing to system(),
    so URL-encoded payloads work transparently.
